[ar:MP3 同步字幕版（美音）]
[ti:Volcanoes]
[by:更多学习内容，请到VeryCD.com搜索“露珠”]
[00:10.03]Why does Tazieff risk his life like this? | 为什么塔捷耶夫要这样冒生命危险？
[00:15.75]Haroun Tazieff, the Polish scientist, has spent his lifetime studying active volcanoes and deep caves in all parts of the world. | 波兰科学家哈鲁恩·塔捷耶夫花了毕生精力研究世界各地的活火山和深洞。
[00:27.85]In 1948, he went to Lake Kivu in the Congo to observe a new volcano which he later named Kituro. | 1948年他去了刚果的基伍湖，观察一座新火山，后来他给它命名为基图罗。
[00:39.75]Tazieff was able to set up his camp very close to the volcano while it was erupting violently. | 当火山猛烈喷发时，塔捷耶夫得以把营地扎在离火山很近的地方。
[00:49.28]Though he managed to take a number of brilliant photographs, he could not stay near the volcano for very long. | 尽管他设法拍了一些精彩的照片，却不能在火山附近停留太久。
[00:58.83]He noticed that a river of liquid rock was coming towards him. | 他发现一股岩浆正向他流来。
[01:03.93]It threatened to surround him completely, but Tazieff managed to escape just in time. | 岩浆眼看就要将他团团围住，但塔捷耶夫设法及时逃脱了。
[01:12.79]He waited until the volcano became quiet and he was able to return two days later. | 他等到火山平静下来，两天后得以返回。
[01:20.47]This time, he managed to climb into the mouth of Kituro so that he could take photographs and measure temperatures. | 这次他设法爬进了基图罗火山口，以便拍摄照片和测量温度。
[01:30.92]Tazieff has often risked his life in this way. | 塔捷耶夫经常这样冒生命危险。
[01:35.69]He has been able to tell us more about active volcanoes than any man alive. | 他能告诉我们的活火山情况比任何在世的人都多。
